\includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{figures/paper/fig3_factorial_grid.pdf}
\caption{Factorial experiment summary. Each cell shows final evaluation return and $\nve$ status. Trained $\dt$-embedding is the sole factor that separates collapsed (red) from healthy (green) configurations.}
\label{fig:factorial_grid}
\end{figure}

When the $\dt$-embedding is present but \emph{untrained} (fixed random projection), value dynamics remain healthy: exp\_008a reaches 777.7 ($\nve = 0.59\times$) and exp\_008c reaches 240.9 ($\nve = 0.58\times$), with no pathological overestimation.  This identifies \emph{training} of the temporal embedding---not its architectural presence---as the causal factor: the untrained embedding provides a temporal signal without co-adapting with the reward head.

